    {
      "actor": "codex-archive-definition",
      "kind": "progress",
      "op_id": "20261006T235219.386531Z-p24284-c0000-r076c-ha6bf3d",
      "text": "Confirmed remaining default-workaround gap2026-10-06 during archive source9e5618b8 qualification: laws crossProject build.sbt818 does not apply commonSettings (its Munit/Discipline dependencies deliberately live in main scope), so Test/javaOptions never receives forkHandshakeOptions653\u2013661. ApiAudit.settings correctly preserves forkOptions.runJVMOptions; the missing law setting, not audit option replacement, causes the instrumented lawsJVM fork to omit preferIPv6Addresses. CI is absent in this local environment. Exact fork18816 waits in ObjectInputStream.readStreamHeader, sbt18492 waits ForkTests.Acceptor.accept, both idle; thread dumps /private/tmp/eyes4s-archive-definition-law-threads.txt and -law-parent-threads.txt, failed audit log -audit-handshake.log. No source mutation while gate is frozen; resume uses process-scoped JAVA_TOOL_OPTIONS=-Djava.net.preferIPv6Addresses=true. Next bounded fix: apply handshake options to laws test JVMs without moving published law dependencies into test scope, verify forked audit launch and complete local gate. Do not close the default-workaround mote while this gap remains.",
      "ts": "2026-10-06T23:52:19.386531Z"
    },
    {
      "actor": "codex-studio-followups",
      "kind": "progress",
      "op_id": "20261007T004150.234566Z-p18035-c0000-rac70-h870ef6",
      "text": "Bounded missing-laws option inheritance fix is implemented on work/studio-followups, commit 6eb8660e, slice bd-01M49VP8GD3EMV6WAZ1KA2D5ZR now in review. A default audit-instrumented lawsJVM fork passed with all manual JVM override environment variables removed; CI options remain unchanged. Full default landing-gate evidence is still required for this parent. Do not count the focused fork as a complete gate.",
      "ts": "2026-10-07T00:41:50.234566Z"
    },
    {
      "actor": "codex-polish-landing",
